# What ships to the ComfyUI registry is what a USER needs to run the node. Everything
# below is development apparatus and is excluded deliberately.
#
# The immediate reason is concrete: tests/test_migration.py imports web/lib/migrate.js
# and executes it under node via subprocess, which is a legitimate way
# to test shipped JS and also exactly the pattern an automated malware scanner flags.
# 0.3.0 contained no subprocess/exec/eval anywhere and went Active; 0.3.3 and 0.3.4 shipped
# that file and both sat at NodeVersionStatusPending. Keeping the apparatus out of the zip
# is the right call regardless of the scanner: it is 12 files a user never runs.

tests/
conftest.py
.gitignore
